00:09:06.990 --> 00:09:10.380
but The Conference Board
saying the decrease reflected

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:13.830
large drops in confidence
for households age 35 to 54.

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:15.210
Those are the most important household.

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:17.790
Those are prime earners,
AKA prime workers.

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:22.680
And for households earning
$35,000 a year or more.

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:24.633
A lot of confidence being lost there.

00:09:25.521 --> 00:09:28.050
That's big, and that's
gonna make a difference.

00:09:28.050 --> 00:09:29.430
Also, housing.

00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:31.860
Housing has played a big role
in the overall inflation story

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:34.470
because the Fed can have a
direct impact on housing.

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:36.270
By raising rates, they
make it more expensive

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:37.103
to get a mortgage,

00:09:37.103 --> 00:09:39.090
make it more expensive
for companies to borrow

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:40.830
to maybe get some of that
commercial real estate.

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:43.350
Well, wanna throw another
chart up here on your screen

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:45.810
and that is existing home sales.

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:47.730
Now, you're seeing the
number of existing homes

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.490
purchased each month decline,
decline, decline, decline,

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:53.490
until up last month, you see
that number rising higher.

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:56.490
That's a 14.5% increase year-over-year

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:57.660
from the previous year.

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:58.980
Now, what does that mean?

00:09:58.980 --> 00:10:00.870
It means folks are still
going out buying homes,

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:03.150
taking out a mortgage,
doing exactly the opposite

00:10:03.150 --> 00:10:05.400
of what the Fed wants
when it's raising rates

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:06.600
to try and get the economy

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:08.940
and trying to get inflation under control.

00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:12.000
Well, that's not a great
sign for the overall economy

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.070
because it means the
Fed may have to do more,

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:15.690
means what it's doing isn't working.

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:17.670
So that chart just kind of illustrates

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:21.060
what we're seeing from
overall housing purchases.

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:23.590
You saw housing slowing down,
prices were coming down.

00:10:23.590 --> 00:10:25.680
Well, prices are starting to pick back up.

